I read some nethack review, where the Castle \WoW was 
described as an artifact.  This gave me an idea, that it 
actually could become an artifact.  Found early, it 
can really screw up your game.  Yesterday I found one
in a chest, 3 squares away from the entrance to the dungeon.
I wished for speed boots, dragon scale mail, gauntlets of
power, helm of brilliance, and two magic markers.  The day
before, I had a rogue with more or less the same equipment,
but all of it found (except dragon scale).  And that game
was actually much funner.  Early wands of wishing just make 
the game too unbalanced.  I mean, 14 wishes in one game 
is much too much.  They almost become abundant, and you 
start wishing for ordinary stuff, like t-shirts.  It just
spoils all the fun that you can out of it.  
Now to the point.
Wand of Wishing, as one and only, found in the heavily guarded
castle, being the greatest prize in the whole game.  That 
makes it worth playing!  There could be some nice story behind
it, like a strong character holding it, making it a little 
similar to the quest.  What do you think about this?

